  "question": {
    "text": "The nucleus of an atom is spherical. The relation between radius of the nucleus and mass number <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is given by <math><mtext>1.25</mtext><mo>×</mo><mtext>1</mtext><msup><mrow><mtext>0</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mtext>13</mtext></mrow></msup><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> . If radius of atom is one <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Å</mi></math> and the mass number is 64, then the fraction of the atomic volume that is occupied by the nucleus is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow></msup></math> . Calculate <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>",
    "image": null
